ithub.com/users/Venosta-web/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Venosta-web/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Venosta-web/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-20T11:29:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T11:29:32Z","body":"Reproduced on 4.7.2.stable (mono, official build, Linux, Wayland via a nested headless `kwin_wayland --virtual`). About 1 in 3 automated runs hang after `SceneTree.quit()`. An all-thread gdb dump of a hung exit matches the description: the main thread is in `pthread_join` on \"Wayland Events\", which sits in `poll()`, and every other thread is idle in futex waits. An idle compositor makes it far more frequent, because no further event ever arrives to wake the poll.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6289841262/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]